1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
Listen to a talk in an archaeology class.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:12,600
Man: For decades, archaeologists believed that complex societies and the monumental architecture,

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,380
the large buildings signifying them,

4
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:21,880
only emerged after agriculture, and that farming was essential for societal development.

5
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:25,160
After all, before agriculture developed,

6
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,680
people tended not to settle in a single place

7
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:31,280
but moved from place to place in search of food.

8
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,900
We call such people nomadic hunter gatherers.

9
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:40,620
They were continuously on the move to hunt and collect food.

10
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,820
And for people who aren't settled,

11
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,060
it was more practical to live in small

12
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:49,960
mobile groups rather than in complex societies

13
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:51,880
Or so it was believed.

14
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:59,640
But the excavation of the ancient site of Gobekli Tepe threw a wrench in this whole story.

15
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:04,080
Gobekli Tepe, dating back about 11,000 years,

16
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:09,560
consists of multiple massive pillars arranged in circles

17
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,740
and is considered the world's oldest known temple.

18
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:21,460
Remarkably, it predates the earliest evidence of agriculture in the area by several thousand years.

19
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:26,240
This suggests spiritual practices, not agriculture

20
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:29,220
may have caused early communities to form.

21
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:33,180
Many scholars interpret the site as a ceremonial center,

22
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:38,240
a periodic gathering place for nomadic hunter gatherers.

23
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:45,680
More recently, archaeologists there did find traces of things like food processing areas,

24
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,540
stone tools for grinding grains,

25
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:55,760
as well as actual plant residues Yet these residues come from local wild grains,

26
00:01:56,100 --> 00:02:02,200
not domesticated crops, and the structures may not indicate year-round habitation.

27
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:06,880
So while Gobekli Tepe might have hosted temporary gatherings,

28
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:15,100
the evidence still supports the idea that spiritual practices played a central role in early societal development.
